  "scope": "Each T and R is the total transmitted or reflected fraction for the indicated native axial drive. The comparator matches normalized-section displacements by reciprocal mass overlap. Direct comparisons subtract the reference fraction from the candidate and divide by the reference for relative changes. The double difference is the two-layer thickness contrast minus the one-layer thickness contrast. Body layers and compatible port discretization change together.",
  "limits": "Finite saved calculations at one frequency with the original physical sections and end planes. Normalized coordinates are used only for displacement matching; T and R are fractions of native incident power. This single-drive comparison leaves all-channel and complex-response failures in force. Weak reflection and relative changes near zero remain sensitive to discretization. Spatial and frequency convergence, a reflection floor, and continuous branch identity remain unresolved. The four-map increment gives no continuum error bound or guaranteed thickness-effect sign."
